{
  "notes": {
    "* header/messageId@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's type restricts messageId to the uuid pattern [a-zA-Z0-9\\-]+; the workbook gives min=36, max=36 alone, so the generated XSD is looser.",
    "* header/messageType@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's shared pattern ([RPCIXH][0-9]{3}) admits H, so the e-Hospitalization values pass; the generated XSD fixes each value and applies the workbook's an class instead. The same pattern leaves out D and L (HEL-27).",
    "* header/senderISName@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The workbook gives chars=an, so the generated XSD keeps a system's name to Latin letters, digits, hyphen and space; today's shared header had no class. A Cyrillic name would be refused: a question for the spec team (HEL-26).",
    "* contents/hospitalization/dischargeDiagnosis order unexplained": "Real drift, and a wire difference (HEL-26). Today's diagnosisFull extends diagnosisBasic, so note comes after the basic fields and before use rank clinicalStatus verificationStatus onsetDateTime; the workbook lists note last.",
    "* contents/hospitalization/comorbidity order unexplained": "Real drift, and a wire difference (HEL-26). Today's diagnosisFull extends diagnosisBasic, so note comes after the basic fields and before use rank clinicalStatus verificationStatus onsetDateTime; the workbook lists note last.",
    "* contents/hospitalization/dischargeDiagnosis/additionalCode cardinality unexplained": "Real drift. The shared diagnosisBasic allows one additional code; the workbook any number.",
    "* contents/hospitalization/comorbidity/additionalCode cardinality unexplained": "Real drift. The shared diagnosisBasic allows one additional code; the workbook any number.",
    "* contents/hospitalization/dischargeDiagnosis/note@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today 4000 characters; the workbook max=2000 on these diagnoses, 4000 elsewhere (HEL-24).",
    "* contents/hospitalization/comorbidity/note@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today 4000 characters; the workbook max=2000 on these diagnoses, 4000 elsewhere (HEL-24).",
    "* contents/hospitalization/epicrisis/dischargingPhysician/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/accommodation/attendingPhysician/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/epicrisis/dischargingPhysician/email@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today's email type has the pattern [^@]+@[^.]+\\..+; the workbook gives max=255 alone.",
    "* contents/hospitalization/sickLeave/number@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today exactly 12 characters; the workbook max=12.",
    "* contents/hospitalization/sickLeave/daysBefore@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The workbook types it Unsigned Int, so 0 is allowed; today's type is positiveInteger.",
    "* contents/accommodation/ward@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today any string; the workbook max=13, chars=n.",
    "* contents/practiceNumber@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today exactly 10 digits; the workbook max=10, chars=n.",
    "* contents/newborn/identifier@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today up to 255 characters; the workbook min=10, max=10, chars=an.",
    "* contents/birth/newborn/identifier@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. Today up to 255 characters; the workbook min=10, max=10, chars=an.",
    "* contents/error/description cardinality unexplained": "Real drift. The shared error type allows one description; the workbook any number.",
    "* contents/error/description@value value-type unexplained": "Real drift. The shared error description holds 2000 characters; the workbook min=1, max=255.",
    "* header/senderISName only-published unexplained": "Real drift. Today's shared header requires senderISName in every message, responses included; the workbook lists it in requests only. NHIS sends the responses, so a vendor only reads them, but a response without it is refused by today's XSD."
  },
